<p>Claude is no longer just a chat interface. Anthropic now positions Claude across coding, research, agents and professional work, and the model family changes quickly. This guide is accurate as of September 2026, but model names, limits and availability can change. citeturn681177search8turn681177search5</p>
<h2>What is Claude?</h2><p>Claude is Anthropic's family of AI models and products for general reasoning, coding, research and agent-style work. Anthropic's 2026 releases include Sonnet 5 and Opus 5, alongside Claude Code and other agentic products. citeturn681177search2turn681177search5turn418603search3</p>
<h2>Which Claude models should you know about?</h2><p>Model names change often, so avoid building your workflow around a static list. Anthropic's current public newsroom identifies Claude Opus 5 and Claude Sonnet 5 as major 2026 releases, with Opus positioned for higher-end work and Sonnet focused on strong agentic performance at a lower cost level. citeturn681177search5turn681177search3</p>
<h2>What can Claude do well?</h2><p>Useful Claude workloads include long-form writing, analysis, coding, document work, research and tasks that need repeated tool use. Claude 4 introduced tool use during extended thinking and parallel tool use, while later releases pushed further into agentic coding and professional work. citeturn214417search9turn681177search3</p>
<h2>What is Claude Code?</h2><p>Claude Code is Anthropic's coding agent built around a developer's working environment. Its CLI supports interactive sessions, non-interactive print mode, resuming conversations, model selection, permission modes and MCP configuration. citeturn214417search6</p>
<h2>How does Claude Research work?</h2><p>Research can conduct multiple searches, explore different angles and use connected work context when integrations are enabled. Anthropic says it returns cited findings so the underlying sources can be checked. citeturn206364search3turn206364search8</p>
<h2>Can Claude use Google Workspace?</h2><p>When supported integrations are connected, Claude can use information from services such as Gmail, Google Calendar and Google Docs as part of research and work tasks. Exact availability depends on the account and plan. citeturn206364search3turn206364search8</p>
<h2>How should you choose between Claude models?</h2><p>Start with task difficulty and cost rather than the model name alone. Use a stronger model for complex reasoning, long-running coding or difficult research; use a faster or less expensive model for routine classification, rewriting and high-volume tasks. Test your own workload because benchmark differences do not always predict your real work.</p>
<h2>How do you get better results from Claude?</h2><p>Give it the job, context, constraints and output format. For research, define a date range and evidence rules. For coding, define what can change and how it should be tested. For writing, provide audience, goal and examples of the desired voice rather than asking for “good content.”</p>
<h2>What should you not assume about Claude?</h2><p>Do not assume every model has the same context, speed, tool access, limits or availability. Anthropic changes these details as products evolve. Check the current official documentation before choosing a model for a production workload. citeturn418603search3</p>
<h2>Where does Claude fit in an SEO workflow?</h2><p>Claude can help with content research, technical audits, log analysis, schema review, large-scale editing and code-based SEO automation. Use it as a working assistant that can inspect evidence and execute defined tasks, not as an automatic source of truth.</p>
